<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grigol of Khandzta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">759–861</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Gregory of Khandzta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grigol of Khandzta was a Georgian monk and saint who founded the monastery of Khandzta in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klarjeti">Klarjeti</a> and organised a network of monasteries in the south-western borderlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Supported by the Bagratid princes, his foundations became centres of learning, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> copying and church building. His life, written by Giorgi Merchule in 951, is a key source for early Bagratid Georgia.</p></div>
